      "englishText": "Samasyā2 :  bhagnDpyabhagnD mama pushpamDlD\n\n(My garland of flowers — broken yet not broken)\n(The metre used by the Samasyā is IndravajrD.The Avadhānī too must compose his śloka in the same metre)\n\nThe Bell: (rings for the 3rd time)\n\nAprastutaprasanga: O dear Avadhānī, are you capable of weaving a garland? Have you ever practiced at home?\n\nAvadhānī: You mean making flower garlands? If I don't have anything to do, I\n\nmake garlands of flowery words.3 Sometimes I also prepare a flower garland made of flowers of devotion and offer it to God in the form of a poetic composition.\n\nAprastutaprasanga: But now your task is to mend a broken garland.\n\nAvadhānī: Yes, I will mend the flower garland of a broken heart with the help of a proper understanding.\n\nVyastākṣarī: I have a śloka in my mind, in which the fifth syllable is 'ma'.\n\n2Samasya, 'problem', from root 'as' and suffix 'sam', means 'to put together', 'to be made entire'. Thus a part of a verse to be completed. \n 3The Avadhānī is a passionate poet too.",
