      "englishText": "Eshu: Today the Department of Sanskrit (of Pondicherry University) has arranged a joint seminar with the Veda Pratisthanam. Please describe the aims and objectives of this seminar to this gathering. \n\nAvadhānī: (composes the śloka in Anushtup metre):\n'shrutisDram samDkirnam vivicya hitakankshayD\nlokasya shreyase sarve...'\n\n(Delving deep, with the desire to do good for the benefit of all, the scattered essence of the Vedas..)\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 6th time)\n\nAprastutaprasanga: (interrupts the Avadhānī when he utters 'sarve' (all), creating a wordplay): Are you doing a survey (here)?\n\nAvadhānī: Yes, all Pandits here have come to do a survey of what is there in the Vedas. (He\n\ncontinues with the śloka he had started): '.... shreyase sarve cinvanti vibudhā iha'\n\n(for the Good of people all pandits here pluck...)\n\nVyastākṣarī: The eleventh syllable is 'dra'.\n\nAvadhānī: 'dra'\n\nVyastākṣarī: The 16th syllable is 'rah'.\n\nAvadhānī: 'rah!'\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 7th time) \n\nPresident: The Avadhānī has answered once all the questions which were asked. The first round is herewith completed and I request the Avadhānī to start the second round. \n( The Avadhānī must remember all the questions asked, the tasks given and the lines composed by him in the first round and continue from there.)",
