      "englishText": "Eshu: Earlier the aims of our assembly (in Pondicherry University) have been revealed by you. The government know about the importance of our assembly, and it has decided to make Sanskrit an official language. Mandana (Mishra) and Vachaspati (Mishra) (two scholars present) are very happy about it. Please describe this.\n\nAvadhānī: (answers with a complete verse in Anushtup metre)\n\nvDchaspateh vachostyaiva muko vDchaspatiyate/\nmandanena kritam mishram samskritena samam samam//\t\t\t\n(The speech of Vachaspati transmutes verily the dumb into the lord  of speech Mandana has brought about an all-encompassing synthesis  through the power of Sanskrit)\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 13th time.)\n \n(Avadhānī continues) With Sanskrit, Mandana Mishra has brought everything that is to say, Indianness, Indian people, etc. into the domain of Sanskrit. So who could be a better person than him? Similarly Vachaspati Mishra has said that if Sanskrit and the essence of the Veda could be communicated to all people, then even a dumb person will get the power of speech. He himself is a living example16. So if we understand the essence of the Vedas, we all — now comparable to dumb beings — will become masters over speech. Knowing the secret of the Veda, we will become filled with intelligence. We will, in the wide vision of Sri Aurobindo, always experience the divine life.\n\n16The literal meaning of \"Vachaspati\" is 'the Lord of Speech'.",
