      "englishText": "Eshu: One hears much about a place called Konasiva, situated at quite a distance from your native place. When I remembered the Coconut trees, I had a desire to go there. Not only me but we all want to go there. Without delay, I request you now, to describe this place through words.\n\t\nPresident: However nowadays the Coconut trees have disappeared. Do you want him to describe the original spot or the place as it looks like today?\n\nAvadhānī: They are eager to see the place. So I will show them what is worth seeing.\n\nPresident: Then show the original scene.\n\nAvadhānī: (composes a verse in Mālinī— a fifteen-syllabled metre)\n   \t          \nsaphalabahulanDrikelakelivilolDh\nvipulavividhasasyashyDmalDsundarDngyah/\namalapuratale yDh purvadrshyDh \nThe Bell: (sounds for the 20th time)\n(continues) bhuvah tDh...\n\n(A site graced with many kinds of Coconut trees laden with fruit,swaying gently with widely stretching fields of various lavish crops,beautiful to watch. This pure place on Earth was Amalapura of olden days...)",
